<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- ⚠️ BUILT-IN SECTIONS ARE NAMED, THIRD-PARTY ONES ARE FILENAMES, AND
       GETTING THAT BACKWARDS BREAKS THE INSTALL ITSELF — not just the order.

       Listing the built-ins by their bundle FILENAMES (Introduction.bundle,
       TargetSelect.bundle, …) produced a scrambled sidebar on a real run —
       "Set Up Keld, Introduction, Destination Select, Summary, Installation
       Type, Read Me, License, Installation" — and the install then failed at
       the end with an EMPTY message and `IFDInstallController state = 0` in
       /var/log/install.log, having never written a payload or run a script.
       An installation sequenced out of order fails exactly that way: instantly,
       with nothing to report.

       The names below are Installer.app's own: the binary carries bare
       "Introduction", "ReadMe", "License", "Target", "PackageSelection",
       "Install" and "Summary" beside the .bundle filenames, and note that the
       one whose file is TargetSelect.bundle is named just "Target" — which is
       what shows the two are different namespaces rather than aliases.

       KeldSetup is OUR bundle, so it is the filename, and it sits before
       "Install" because a section placed after it never appears at all: the
       plugin's host process stops the moment installation completes (measured
       2026-09-14). -->
  <key>SectionOrder</key>
  <array>
    <string>Introduction</string>
    <string>ReadMe</string>
    <string>License</string>
    <string>Target</string>
    <string>PackageSelection</string>
    <string>KeldSetup.bundle</string>
    <string>Install</string>
    <string>Summary</string>
  </array>
</dict>
</plist>
